{"execute":{"doc":1,"cmd":{"Write":{"PasteMarkdown":{"text":"Amara Lindqvist\n\nSenior Product Designer\n\nLeeds, UK · +44 7700 900 418 · amara.lindqvist@example.com · amaralindqvist.example\n\n# Profile\n\nProduct designer with eight years in health and booking products. I turn messy services into calm, accessible journeys, back decisions with research, and build the systems teams need to ship consistently.\n\n# Experience\n\n## Senior Product Designer, Brightwell Clinics\n\nLeeds · 2022 – present\n\n- Led the redesign of appointment booking across web and mobile apps (1.4 million users)\n- Cut median booking time from 4 minutes to 85 seconds; help-line calls fell by 48 %\n- Built and maintain the design system shared by four product teams\n\n## Product Designer, Tessellate Travel\n\nManchester · 2019 – 2022\n\n- Designed the group booking flow that now accounts for 22 % of revenue\n- Introduced fortnightly usability testing and a research repository\n\n## UX Designer, Copperline Agency\n\nManchester · 2017 – 2019\n\n- Delivered service design and prototypes for twelve public and charity clients\n\n# Education\n\n## MA Interaction Design, University of Northbridge\n\n2016 – 2017 · Distinction\n\n## BA Graphic Communication, Pennine College of Art\n\n2013 – 2016 · First-class honours\n\n# Selected projects\n\n**Booking for everyone** — a booking journey tested with 60 patients aged 70 and over; shortlisted for the Northern Design Awards 2024.\n\n**Quiet mode** — a low-stimulation version of the clinic app for neurodivergent patients, now used by 38,000 people a month.\n\n# Skills\n\n**Design** — interaction and visual design, prototyping, design systems, accessibility (WCAG 2.2)\n\n**Research** — interviews, usability testing, journey mapping, service blueprints\n\n**Tools** — prototyping and design-system tools, HTML and CSS, research repositories\n\n**Languages** — English (native), Swedish (fluent), French (conversational)\n"}}}}}
